invariant: INV-16
file: pem_files.c
catches: pem_files_host
reason: a host object computes the key's point on ct.h's 16x16
  decomposition whatever its cpu value states. The point is the same. The
  ruling puts the point on the wide P-256 field when the value holds
  CH_CPU_CONSTANT_TIME_MULTIPLY, as p256_sign_cpu signs
  (docs/decisions.md 131). test_key_cpu counts the calls into each copy
  and requires the wide files under the bit.

--- old
#define KEY_WIDEMUL(cpu) widemul_of_cpu(cpu)
--- new
#define KEY_WIDEMUL(cpu) ((void)(cpu), WIDEMUL_NOT_STATED)
